  "testStepWeightsNote": [
    "Milliseconds per step, MEASURED ON GITHUB'S RUNNERS (ubuntu-latest), the",
    "machine CI actually packs for. Each value is the mean of two full CI runs,",
    "read from every shard's own SUMMARY table: Tests #265 (1b4d73c) and #266",
    "(6abb59c), 2026-10-13. #266 was cancelled at the 25-min job timeout, so its",
    "shards 5 and 6 have no SUMMARY; their steps are read from each step's own",
    "PASS line instead, and the one step each was cut off in (integration,",
    "photoset:drive) takes the mean of #264 (79bfd7d) and #265. The thirteen steps",
    "#266 added (lift:auto-test, lift:auto-drive, foam:test, foam:drive, ui:shell,",
    "zoom:drive, findings:test, findings:drive, bend:test, bend:drive,",
    "cut:inside-out, wire:cut-inside-out, wire:cut-yaw) carry #266's time alone,",
    "until a second CI run measures them. Rounded to 50ms above a second.",
    "",
    "The previous table (#232/#233, 2026-09-27, plus local-times-x-1.7 estimates",
    "for each step added after) had drifted to 6,012s against 7,864s on #266. The",
    "estimates were not the worst of it: rotate:handles was declared at 4s and",
    "has run 243-261s in each of #264-#266, scale:card 23s against",
    "~155s, zoom:drive 140s against 294s. Runners also swing: the 186 steps #265",
    "and #266 share summed 5,073s in #265 and 6,946s in #266 (median per-step",
    "ratio 1.36). These weights sum to 6,957s and pack eight shards at 870s",
    "each (six would be 1,160s); a #266-speed run is ~1.13x that.",
    "Steps merged after #167 carry their own branch's estimate until a CI run",
    "measures them: cavity:thickwall 110 (0.08s local; the old page:manifest's floor); page:manifest 4200 (2.4s local x 1.7, rounded up: it launches Chromium for its 1280 x 800 gate now, and was 47); wire:cut-tip 153000 (90s local x 1.7, rounded up); gcode:gscope-zoom 335000 (197s local x 1.7, rounded up); lift:curved-test 91000 and lift:curved-drive 198000 (53s / 116s local, x 1.7, rounded up); support:inside 600 (0.33s local x 1.7, rounded up); wire:cut-redesign 42000 (24.3s local x 1.7, rounded up); shell:v3 70000 (41s local x 1.7, rounded up; shell:v2 was 54000); support:beacons 3100 (1.8s local x 1.7, rounded up); support:gridpack 41000 (24s local x 1.7, rounded up); soften:holes 64000 (37.6s local x 1.7, rounded up); tube:edges 27000 and tube:edges-drive 37500 (15.6s / 21.8s local x 1.7, rounded up); bridge:test 1800 and bridge:drive 61000 (1.04s / 35.6s local, x 1.7, rounded up); support:ui 54000 (31.9s local x 1.7, rounded up); carve:drag 67000 (39.4s local x 1.7, rounded up); tube:neck 34000 (20.0s local x 1.7, rounded up); support:card 107000 (63s local x 1.7, rounded up); lift:plate 346000 (203s local x 1.7, rounded up); lift:any-face 72000 (42s local x 1.7, rounded up); close:test 3600 (2.1s local x 1.7, rounded up; 2100 before the pick walked and the Cut fixture joined); crop:shapes 77000 (45s local x 1.7, rounded up); crop:engine 31000 (18s local x 1.7, rounded up); crop:drive 190000 (112s local x 1.7, rounded up; crop:move and wire:crop-move are retired with Move); mold:test 22500 and mold:drive 76000 (13.1s / 44.5s local x 1.7, rounded up); repair:loop 38000 (22.4s local x 1.7, rounded up); patch:test 8000 (4.6s local x 1.7, rounded up); findings:drive 180000 (it gained section 9: 106s local x 1.7, rounded up); pull:test 51000 and pull:drive 160000 (30s / 94s local x 1.7, rounded up); grab:drop 169000 (99s local x 1.7, rounded up); lift:assembly 92000 (54s local x 1.7, rounded up); camera:leash 300 (0.18s local x 1.7, rounded up); gscope:shell 52000 (30.6s local x 1.7, rounded up); gscope:take 94000 (55s local x 1.7, rounded up); support:exposed 81000 (60s on the cloud box, which ran the old test in 29s against its recorded 23s, so ~47s local x 1.7, rounded up; it was 23s before supports-followups: the gaps between pads, the shelf / arch / tunnel sections and a through-hole fixture that now holds 26 points, not 9); wire:cut-mitre-drag 96000 (56s local x 1.7, rounded up); stock:shelf 140000 (82s local, with another suite running beside it, x 1.7, rounded up); lift:curved-surface 10300 (6s local x 1.7, rounded up) and lift:curved-surface-drive 600 (it skips, with a notice, when the two real files in tools/fixtures-local/ are absent, as on CI; with them it is minutes); overlap:drive 70000 (41s local x 1.7, rounded up); pick:release 185000 (109s local x 1.7, rounded up); support:workflow 360000 (~210s local x 1.7, rounded up; it was 40000 before it gained the real 60 s watchdog wait and the wedge section); support:index 85000 (~50s local, with other work running, x 1.7, rounded up); connect:test 27000 and connect:drive 210000 (15.8s / 123s local x 1.7, rounded up; the anchor-point ticket took them from 22500 / 155000; Sag and Ends had taken them from 15000 / 60000).",
    "",
    "Only the shard packing in",
    "tools/run-tests.mjs reads them (and run-tests-parallel.mjs prints their sum).",
    "No test behaviour depends on them: a step missing from this table is packed",
    "at the median, not skipped - and that is not harmless (below).",
    "",
    "WHY THEY ARE CI TIMES, NOT LOCAL ONES. The table before #232/#233 was measured on one",
    "local 4-core box (2026-09-20/21). On the runners the suite is ~3,860s, not",
    "the table's 2,280s - 1.7x in total - and per step the error was far larger:",
    "gcode:gscope-cornercam 12s -> 68s, gcode:gscope-support 20s -> 104s,",
    "seat:overhang 7s -> 48s. Ten steps were missing outright (topbar:accordion,",
    "95s on a runner, was packed as a median step). Under the real times the old",
    "packing put shards 5 and 6 at ~800s of tests, 14.2-14.7 min with setup",
    "against a 15-min job timeout: the cancellations of Tests #231 and #233 were",
    "that, not a failing test. Repacked on those numbers every shard was 652s.",
    "",
    "A SNAPSHOT, NOT A CONSTANT. Steps get slower as they grow and runners vary:",
    "between #232 and #233, same steps, the per-step ratio had median 1.01 but",
    "p10 0.68 and p90 1.54 - which is why this is a mean of two runs, not one.",
    "The symptom of drift is uneven shard times, and past a point a shard hitting",
    "the job timeout. Re-measure from a green CI run: each shard's log ends with",
    "a SUMMARY table of its steps and times; average two runs, rewrite the block",
    "below, and check `node tools/run-tests.mjs --shard-plan 8`, which prints the",
    "packing they produce and has no wall clock in it at all.",
    "",
    "Locally these are NOT this machine's times (a local box is ~1.7x faster), so",
    "run-tests-parallel.mjs no longer draws a speedup ratio from their sum."
  ],
